2.3.0
A two-item release, and it is small because a consumer MEASURED the premise of its original headline feature and found it did not exist: the `hooks/local/pre-gate.sh` extension point was justified by "two repos maintain merge scripts reassembling run-gate.sh", and the count is one repo, one file, one 13-line insertion, with the second repo carrying no splice at all — so the extension point is CANCELLED rather than shipped as a permanent surface for a single deviation. What replaces it costs no new mechanism: a chained `**Gate**: bash preflight.sh && <real gate>` already works, and the one thing it could not express — a terminal exit, because a chained preflight's 78 becomes the gate command's rc and run-gate.sh's clamp collapses it to 1 — is expressible with `RUN_GATE_TERMINAL`, which run-gate.sh already exports. So v2.3.0 DOCUMENTS that as a public contract (print the remedy to stderr, touch `$RUN_GATE_TERMINAL`, exit 78) with a verbatim worked example in `docs/verification.md`, and pins it with a consistency assertion that the export still precedes the `bash -c "$GATE_CMD"` line plus a both-arms fixture (marker touched + 78 ⇒ terminal, remedy last, retry advice suppressed; 78 without the touch ⇒ clamped to 1, retry advice present). The honest cost is named rather than discovered: `RUN_GATE_TERMINAL` can no longer be renamed freely — accepted because it is already exported into every gate command's environment, so consumers can depend on it today whether or not it is written down. Second item: `hooks/enforce-delegation.sh` now strips HEREDOC BODIES before classifying a command, because a body is data with an explicit terminator and authoring a document containing `npm test` is not running one. `hooks/lib/git-cmd.sh` is deliberately untouched — the three fail-CLOSED git gates scan the whole command string on purpose so `bash -c "git push origin main"` cannot evade them, and quoted-literal stripping stays rejected because separating that from `echo "git push origin main"` needs a maintained wrapper allowlist whose every gap is an evasion channel that is closed today; both accepted false positives are now asserted POSITIVELY, so an "improvement" that strips quoted literals turns the suite red instead of passing quietly.
